---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/ui/Container.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Kitchen Table Wonders"
  description="What Kitchen Table Wonders collects, why, and your choices — in plain English. No email or personal data goes to our analytics."
>
  <Container>
    <article class="legal">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 9 September 2026</p>

      <p>
        Kitchen Table Wonders (“we”, “us”, “our”) runs kitchentablewonders.com and sells
        printable digital products. This policy explains what information we collect, why,
        and your choices. We keep it short and plain on purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Kitchen Table Wonders, contactable at <a href="mailto:hello@kitchentablewonders.com">hello@kitchentablewonders.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Email address</strong> — when you sign up for our free printable Kids’
          Passport, join our email list, or make a purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Order information</strong> — what you bought and when. Payments are
          processed by <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong>, our merchant of record, who handles
          checkout and delivers your files; we do <strong>not</strong> collect or store your
          card details — they do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic usage data</strong> — anonymous information about how the site is
          used, such as which pages are viewed and which buttons are clicked. See
          <a href="#analytics">How we use analytics</a> below for exactly what this does
          and doesn’t include.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The free Kids’ Passport and our email list</h2>
      <p>
        We collect the email address you submit so we can send you the free printable Kids’
        Passport and occasional updates about new country kits. Your email is managed by
        <strong>Kit</strong>, our email provider. You can unsubscribe at any time — every
        email has an unsubscribe link, and it works instantly.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">How we use analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Amplitude</strong>, a third-party analytics service, to understand
        how visitors use our site — for example, which pages are viewed and which buttons
        are clicked — so we can make it better.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Amplitude assigns an <strong>anonymous device identifier</strong> that is stored
          in your browser. We use it to count visits and understand general usage patterns.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do <strong>not</strong> send Amplitude your email address, your name, or any
          other personal information. If you join our email list, that address is handled
          only by Kit — it is never shared with Amplitude.
        </li>
        <li>
          Amplitude uses your IP address only to infer a <strong>coarse location</strong>
          (such as country and city) for aggregate usage statistics. It is not stored in
          full and is never used to identify you.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not use analytics to build advertising profiles about you, and we don’t
          sell your data.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That anonymous identifier is kept in your browser’s local storage (similar to a
        cookie). You can clear it at any time in your browser settings. Browser tracking
        protection or an ad blocker may block our analytics entirely — that’s completely
        fine, and the site works exactly the same either way.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To send you the free download and product you asked for.</li>
        <li>
          To send occasional emails about new country packs, tips, and offers (only if you
          opted in).
        </li>
        <li>To respond to your questions.</li>
        <li>To improve our products and website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information to anyone.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with (service providers only)</h2>
      <p>
        We use trusted third parties to run the business, and share only what’s needed:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong> — our merchant of record, which processes payment
          and delivers your digital products.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Kit</strong> — to send the emails you opted into.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Amplitude</strong> — anonymous usage data only, as described above.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Instagram, Pinterest, and similar platforms</strong> — if you interact
          with us there. Each has its own privacy policy governing your data on their
          systems.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our products are made for families to use together, but our website and purchases
        are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        children under 13. If you believe a child has given us their information, contact
        us and we’ll delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Unsubscribe anytime — every email has an unsubscribe link, and it works instantly.
        </li>
        <li>
          Clear the anonymous analytics identifier at any time in your browser settings, or
          block analytics entirely with tracking protection or an ad blocker.
        </li>
        <li>
          We keep your information only as long as needed for the purposes above, or as
          required by law.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies and similar storage</h2>
      <p>
        Our site and our tools may use cookies or similar browser storage to remember
        preferences and measure traffic. You can control or disable these in your browser
        settings; some features may not work as well without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect your information, but no method of transmission
        over the internet is 100% secure, and we can’t guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy; we’ll change the “Last updated” date above when we do.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about your privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@kitchentablewonders.com">hello@kitchentablewonders.com</a>.</p>

      <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back home</a></p>
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .legal { max-width: 70ch; margin-inline: auto; padding-block: 3rem 4rem; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem);
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }
  .updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--navy); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
